MICROSERVICES E-COMMERCE AWS EKS PROJECT
=========================================

1. CLONE REPOSITORY

git clone https://github.com/gsharma1298/micro-service.git


2. CONFIGURE AWS

aws configure


3. PROJECT DIRECTORY

ls
cd micro-service



ls


4. CREATE S3 BUCKETS / TERRAFORM STATE

cd s3-buckets/

terraform init

terraform plan

terraform apply -auto-approve


5. CREATE NETWORK INFRASTRUCTURE

cd ../terraform_main_ec2

terraform init

terraform plan

terraform apply -auto-approve


6. CHECK TERRAFORM STATE

terraform state list


7. SWITCH TO ROOT USER

sudo -i


8. CHECK DEVOPS TOOLS

git --version

java -version

jenkins --version

terraform -version

mvn -v

kubectl version --client --short

eksctl version

helm version --short

docker --version

trivy --version


9. GET JENKINS ADMIN PASSWORD

cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword


10. UPDATE EKS KUBECONFIG

aws eks --region us-east-1 update-kubeconfig --name project-eks


11. CHECK EKS NODES

kubectl get nodes


12. CHECK ECR REPOSITORIES

aws ecr describe-repositories --region us-east-1


========================
ARGOC D
========================

13. CREATE ARGOCD NAMESPACE

kubectl create namespace argocd


14. INSTALL ARGOCD

kubectl apply -n argocd -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/argoproj/argo-cd/stable/manifests/install.yaml


15. CHECK ARGOCD PODS

kubectl get pods -n argocd


16. CHECK KUBERNETES NODES

kubectl get nodes


17. CHECK ALL ARGOCD RESOURCES

kubectl get all -n argocd


18. EDIT ARGOCD SERVICE

kubectl edit svc argocd-server -n argocd

CHANGE:

type: ClusterIP

TO:

type: LoadBalancer


19. GET ARGOCD LOAD BALANCER

kubectl get svc argocd-server -n argocd


20. GET ARGOCD ADMIN PASSWORD

kubectl get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -n argocd -o jsonpath="{.data.password}" | base64 -d && echo


